<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <%- include('partials/head', { title: 'About Us', description: 'Meet the passionate travel team behind Iberian Chronicles, uncovering the soul, culture, and hidden corners of Spain and Portugal.', extraCSS: ['/styles/about.css'] }) %>
</head>
<body>
  <%- include('partials/header') %>

  <main id="page-main" tabindex="-1">
    <div class="page-container">

      <section class="about-section" aria-labelledby="about-hero-title">
        <h2 class="page-title" id="about-hero-title">Meet the minds behind Iberian Chronicles</h2>
        <p class="body-text">
          We are a small travel editorial team exploring Spain and Portugal with a slower, more local lens.
          Our focus is on memorable routes, cultural detail, food, and the kind of places people talk about
          after the trip ends.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="about-section">
        <h2 class="page-title">Our story</h2>
        <p class="body-text">
          We did not just want to visit the Iberian Peninsula; we wanted to understand it.
        </p>
        <p class="body-text">
          Iberian Chronicles was born from a shared belief that the best travel stories aren't found on postcard
          racks, but off the beaten path. As a team, we realized that Spain and Portugal are a vast, interconnected
          tapestry of ancient traditions, diverse landscapes, and culinary wonders that deserve deeper exploration.
        </p>
        <p class="body-text">
          Whether we're uncovering a centuries-old festival in a remote village, sharing the complex history behind
          a hidden Moorish castle, or tracking down the best local tasca for authentic tapas, our collective goal
          is to capture the true heartbeat of Iberia and share it with curious travelers like you."
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="about-section">
        <h2 class="page-title">What You'll Find Here</h2>
        <p class="body-text">We design our content for travelers who want to move past the typical tourist itineraries.</p>
        <ul class="body-text">
          <li>
            <strong>Curated Slow Travel Guides:</strong> Comprehensive itineraries designed to help you absorb the
            local atmosphere rather than rush through it.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Off-the-Beaten-Path Destinations:</strong> Escaping the crowds to discover hidden white-walled
            villages, pristine natural parks, and secret coastlines.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Culinary Journeys:</strong> Deep dives into regional gastronomic traditions, from the vineyards
            of La Rioja to the traditional bakeries of Lisbon.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Practical Travel Tips:</strong> Honest, actionable advice on local etiquette, languages, and
            budgeting to help plan a seamless adventure.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="about-section" aria-labelledby="about-social-title">
        <h2 class="page-title" id="about-social-title">Follow the journey</h2>
        <p class="body-text">
          Travel is best shared. We post updates, behind-the-scenes notes, and story highlights as we move across
          Spain and Portugal.
        </p>
        <p class="body-text">
          <strong>See the latest posts:</strong> Visit our <a href="/articles">Articles</a> page.
        </p>
        <p class="body-text">
          <strong>Talk to us:</strong> Use the <a href="/contact">Contact Page</a> to suggest a destination or
          collaboration.
        </p>
        <p class="body-text">
          <strong>Social:</strong> Follow <a href="https://twitter.com/IberianChronicles" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">@IberianChronicles</a>
          for short updates from the road.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="about-section">
        <h2 class="page-title">Let's Connect!</h2>
        <p class="body-text">
          Travel is best shared. We'd love to hear about your own adventures or help you plan your upcoming trip.
        </p>
        <p class="body-text">
          <strong>Explore the Blog:</strong> Check out our latest <a href="/articles">Articles</a> for fresh inspiration.
        </p>
        <p class="body-text">
          <strong>Get in Touch:</strong> Have a question or want to collaborate with our team? Head over to the
          <a href="/contact">Contact Page</a>.
        </p>
        <p class="body-text">
          <strong>Join the Community:</strong> Follow along on social media
          <a href="https://twitter.com/IberianChronicles" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">@IberianChronicles</a>
          for live updates and behind-the-scenes moments from our journeys.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="about-section">
        <h2 class="page-title">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

        <article class="faq-item">
          <h3 class="section-heading">Who is behind Iberian Chronicles?</h3>
          <p class="body-text">
            We are a team of passionate travel writers, photographers, and cultural enthusiasts who fell in love
            with the Iberian Peninsula. Instead of just scratching the surface, we pooled our diverse backgrounds
            in history, gastronomy, and sustainable travel to create a comprehensive digital guide dedicated
            entirely to exploring Spain and Portugal deeply.
          </p>
        </article>
        <hr class="faq-divider">

        <article class="faq-item">
          <h3 class="section-heading">How do you choose the destinations you feature?</h3>
          <p class="body-text">
            While we cover iconic highlights like Lisbon, Madrid, and Barcelona, our true passion lies in
            "slow travel." We actively seek out lesser-known white-walled villages, hidden coastal paths,
            regional culinary traditions, and historical sites that are often overlooked by mainstream tourism
            boards. If a place has a unique story, an authentic local food culture, or pristine natural beauty,
            it makes it onto our map.
          </p>
        </article>
        <hr class="faq-divider">

        <article class="faq-item">
          <h3 class="section-heading">Are your itineraries and recommendations sponsored?</h3>
          <p class="body-text">
            Transparency is incredibly important to us. The vast majority of our travels are entirely self-funded
            to ensure our reviews of boutique hotels, local tascas, and tour operators remain completely honest
            and unbiased. If we ever partner with a tourism board or a brand, it will always be explicitly
            disclosed at the top of the article. We only recommend experiences we have personally vetted and
            genuinely love.
          </p>
        </article>
        <hr class="faq-divider">

        <article class="faq-item">
          <h3 class="section-heading">Can we use your photos or content for our own projects?</h3>
          <p class="body-text">
            All photography, writing, and custom maps on this site are the intellectual property of the Iberian
            Chronicles Team unless stated otherwise. If you'd like to feature our work on your website or media
            outlet, please <a href="/contact">drop us a line</a> to discuss licensing. We love collaborating, but
            we strictly protect our creative content!
          </p>
        </article>
        <hr class="faq-divider">

        <article class="faq-item">
          <h3 class="section-heading">How can we collaborate or work with your team?</h3>
          <p class="body-text">
            We welcome partnerships with tourism boards, sustainable travel brands, eco-lodges, and cultural
            agencies that align with our slow-travel philosophy. Whether you are looking for content creation,
            editorial features, photography, or digital promotion within the Iberian travel niche, you can reach
            out directly to our team using the <a href="/contact">contact form</a>.
          </p>
        </article>
      </section>

    </div>
  </main>

  <%- include('partials/footer') %>
</body>
</html>